      "claim": "The closely related xanthine A1 antagonist PET tracer [11C]MPDX showed widespread brain distribution in monkey PET imaging, directly demonstrating effective BBB penetration in a species relevant to CNS exposure.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C09"],
      "claim": "[11C]MPDX was reported to penetrate the blood-brain barrier easily in mice, rats, and cats, supporting the CNS access of the same xanthine scaffold as the query.",
